# =============================================================================
# RAG project — ignores SPECIFIC to this subtree.
#
# The repo root (../.gitignore) already covers: __pycache__, *.pyc, .venv/,
# .ipynb_checkpoints/, .vscode/, .cursor/, .env, MENTOR_PROGRESS.md.
# Only what it does NOT cover belongs here.
# =============================================================================

# --- Qdrant local volume — 889 MB ------------------------------------------
# THE ONE THAT WOULD BREAK THE PUSH. GitHub rejects files over 100 MB, and this
# is prototype vectors from ONE document in collections named reg_*_test.
# Derived data: rebuildable from the corpus, and stale the moment the chunker
# changes. A vector store never belongs in git.
qdrant_storage/

# --- parse cache -------------------------------------------------------------
# Gzipped DoclingDocuments keyed by source hash AND docling version. Derived;
# regenerate with `python -m regrag.ingestion.cache --warm`. Would also churn on
# every Docling upgrade, since the version is part of the filename.
data/processed/

# --- test / build artefacts --------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
*.tmp
*.json.gz.tmp

# =============================================================================
# SOURCE PDFs — EXCLUDED BY DECISION (2026-08-21)
# =============================================================================
# 22 MB of published regulation, and redistribution terms differ sharply by
# publisher:
#
#   Fed / eCFR / SR letters   US government works — no restriction
#   BIS / BCBS                covers state "Brief excerpts may be reproduced or
#                             translated provided the source is stated".
#                             A complete 323-page chapter is not a brief excerpt.
#   IFRS 9 (IFRS Foundation)  copyright asserted and actively enforced
#   PRA / Bank of England     usually Open Government Licence, attribution
#
# CONSEQUENCE: a fresh clone has no corpus, so registry validation and every
# file-resolving test FAIL until the PDFs are fetched. Each registry row carries
# a `source_url`, so scripts/fetch_corpus.py can rebuild the corpus from the
# registry — which is a better artefact than the files themselves, because it
# makes the corpus REPRODUCIBLE rather than merely present.
data/**/*.pdf

# Keep the directory structure so a clone knows where the corpus goes.
!data/**/.gitkeep

# =============================================================================
# PROTOTYPE LEFTOVERS
# =============================================================================
# Duplicate of docling.ipynb, kept locally, not worth publishing.
notebooks/Prototype/*Copy*.ipynb
